<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dae Gwang-hyeon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 934</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dae Gwang-hyeon was the crown prince of Balhae, a descendant of its founder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dae-joyeong">Dae Joyeong</a>, who led a large body of refugees to Goryeo after the Khitan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao dynasty</a> destroyed Balhae in 926. King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taejo-of-goryeo">Taejo of Goryeo</a> welcomed him in 934, gave him the royal surname Wang and entered him in the royal family register, as Goryeo presented itself as heir to Goguryeo and Balhae.</p></div>
